# Button — Behavior Spec

## 1. Intent

The Orbit Button is the system's primary mechanism for triggering user-initiated actions. It communicates emphasis through four variants that map to action importance: Primary (the most important action on a surface), Secondary (supporting actions), Ghost (low-emphasis or repetitive actions), and Destructive (irreversible or dangerous actions). A button's variant is always selected relative to the other actions on the same surface — there is no absolute "correct" variant in isolation.

---

## 2. Scope & Boundaries

**In scope:**
- All four variants: Primary, Secondary, Ghost, Destructive
- Two sizes: Default (md) and Small (sm)
- Icon + label layout (icon left or icon right)
- All interaction states: default, hover, focus, active, disabled, loading
- Loading state with Phosphor spinner icon
- As a `<button>` element only

**Out of scope:**
- Icon-only buttons (see ODS-ICONBTN-L2-002)
- Link-style buttons that navigate (use `<a>` styled with Button tokens — not this component)
- Button groups / segmented controls (see ODS-BTNGROUP-L2-003)
- Full-width/block button layout (L3 delivery specs apply spacing; Button provides the component)

---

## 3. States & Variants

### Variants

#### Primary

**When to use:** The single most important, expected action on a given surface. One Primary Button per visible surface. Forms have one. Modals have one. Dashboards may have one per panel.

**When NOT to use:** When there are two equally important actions — neither should be Primary; use Secondary + Primary and consider which is truly the default path. Never for navigation (use a link). Never for destructive actions (use Destructive).

**Visual spec (md size):**

| Property | Token |
|----------|-------|
| Background (default) | color-action-primary |
| Background (hover) | color-action-primary-dark |
| Background (active) | color-action-primary-dark |
| Background (disabled) | color-surface-base |
| Text | color-text-on-action |
| Text (disabled) | color-text-disabled |
| Border | none |
| Padding horizontal | spacing-4 |
| Padding vertical | spacing-2 |
| Border-radius | radius-md |
| Font | typography-label-md |
| Min height | 36px (md), 28px (sm) |
| Min width | 80px |

#### Secondary

**When to use:** Supporting actions that accompany a Primary action. Cancel paired with Submit. Export paired with Create.

**When NOT to use:** When no Primary action is present — if there's only one action and it's not the most important thing on the surface, consider Ghost.

**Visual spec (md size):**

| Property | Token |
|----------|-------|
| Background (default) | color-surface-raised |
| Background (hover) | color-surface-base |
| Background (active) | color-surface-base |
| Background (disabled) | color-surface-base |
| Text | color-text-primary |
| Text (disabled) | color-text-disabled |
| Border | 1px solid color-border-default |
| Border (hover) | 1px solid color-border-strong |
| Border (disabled) | 1px solid color-border-default |
| Padding horizontal | spacing-4 |
| Padding vertical | spacing-2 |
| Border-radius | radius-md |
| Font | typography-label-md |

#### Ghost

**When to use:** Low-emphasis actions. Actions that repeat (e.g., "Edit" on each table row). Secondary navigation actions. "Skip" in onboarding. Dismissing non-critical alerts.

**When NOT to use:** As the only action on a surface — a surface with only Ghost buttons gives users no visual hierarchy signal.

**Visual spec (md size):**

| Property | Token |
|----------|-------|
| Background (default) | transparent |
| Background (hover) | color-surface-base |
| Background (active) | color-surface-base |
| Background (disabled) | transparent |
| Text | color-text-secondary |
| Text (hover) | color-text-primary |
| Text (disabled) | color-text-disabled |
| Border | none |
| Padding horizontal | spacing-3 |
| Padding vertical | spacing-2 |
| Border-radius | radius-md |
| Font | typography-label-md |

#### Destructive

**When to use:** Actions that are irreversible or have significant negative impact — Delete, Revoke access, Permanently remove. Always paired with a confirmation modal (L2: ODS-MOD-L2-001).

**When NOT to use:** For any action that can be undone. For actions that are merely "negative" but reversible (e.g., "Disable" when there's an "Enable" path).

**Visual spec (md size):**

| Property | Token |
|----------|-------|
| Background (default) | color-semantic-error |
| Background (hover) | #B91C1C (darker red — defined as color-semantic-error-dark in L1 v1.1.0) |
| Background (disabled) | color-surface-base |
| Text | color-text-on-action |
| Text (disabled) | color-text-disabled |
| Border | none |
| Padding horizontal | spacing-4 |
| Padding vertical | spacing-2 |
| Border-radius | radius-md |
| Font | typography-label-md |

---

### States

#### Default
Base appearance. No interaction in progress. Refer to variant tables for token values.

#### Hover
Applies on `mouseenter`. Transition: `motion-duration-fast` + `motion-ease-standard` for background color change.

- Primary: background → `color-action-primary-dark`
- Secondary: border → `color-border-strong`
- Ghost: background → `color-surface-base`, text → `color-text-primary`
- Destructive: background → `color-semantic-error-dark`

Cursor: `pointer`.

#### Focus
Applies on keyboard focus via Tab. Focus ring: `0 0 0 2px var(--color-focus-ring)` + `var(--shadow-focus)` outside the button's border-radius boundary.

The focus ring must be visible against all surfaces this button may appear on: `color-surface-base`, `color-surface-raised`, `color-action-primary-subtle`.

#### Active / Pressed
Applies on `mousedown`. Visually identical to hover state. Provides tactile click feedback. Duration: for the duration of the press.

#### Disabled
`aria-disabled="true"` on the `<button>` element. `pointer-events: none`. `cursor: not-allowed` on the parent if a tooltip explains why it's disabled.

Do NOT use the HTML `disabled` attribute alone — it removes the element from the tab order, preventing screen reader users from discovering it and its explanation.

Background: `color-surface-base`. Text: `color-text-disabled`. No border for Primary/Destructive; border `color-border-default` for Secondary.

Opacity: Do not use opacity to achieve the disabled look. Use explicit disabled tokens.

#### Loading
Triggered when the button initiates an async operation.

- Label text is replaced by a Phosphor `SpinnerGap` icon (animated, 16px) with `aria-hidden="true"`
- `aria-busy="true"` is added to the button
- `aria-label` is updated to "Loading..." (or "Saving…" / "Submitting…" if context is known)
- `pointer-events: none` is applied
- Visual appearance matches the Default state (not Disabled) — same background, same text color

---

## 4. Token Usage

| Property | Variant | State | Token |
|----------|---------|-------|-------|
| Background | Primary | Default | color-action-primary |
| Background | Primary | Hover/Active | color-action-primary-dark |
| Background | Primary | Disabled | color-surface-base |
| Background | Secondary | Default | color-surface-raised |
| Background | Secondary | Hover/Active | color-surface-base |
| Background | Ghost | Default | transparent |
| Background | Ghost | Hover/Active | color-surface-base |
| Background | Destructive | Default | color-semantic-error |
| Text | Primary | Default | color-text-on-action |
| Text | Secondary/Ghost | Default | color-text-primary |
| Text | Ghost | Default | color-text-secondary |
| Text | All | Disabled | color-text-disabled |
| Border | Secondary | Default | color-border-default |
| Border | Secondary | Hover | color-border-strong |
| Focus ring | All | Focus | color-focus-ring |
| Focus shadow | All | Focus | shadow-focus |
| Padding (h) md | All | All | spacing-4 |
| Padding (v) md | All | All | spacing-2 |
| Padding (h) sm | All | All | spacing-3 |
| Padding (v) sm | All | All | spacing-1 |
| Border-radius | All | All | radius-md |
| Font | All | All | typography-label-md |
| Icon size | All | All | 16px (Phosphor, matching label baseline) |
| Transition | All | Hover/Focus | motion-duration-fast + motion-ease-standard |

---

## 5. Interaction Contract

### Mouse

| Event | Response |
|-------|----------|
| mouseenter | Enter Hover state (background transition) |
| mouseleave | Return to Default state (background transition) |
| mousedown | Enter Active state |
| mouseup | Trigger onClick handler, return to Hover state |
| click (disabled) | No response. Cursor shows `not-allowed` if tooltip is present. |

### Keyboard

| Key | Response |
|-----|----------|
| Tab | Focus moves to button. Focus ring appears. |
| Shift+Tab | Focus moves away from button. |
| Enter | Triggers onClick handler (same as click) |
| Space | Triggers onClick handler (same as click — required for `<button>` elements) |
| Any other key | No response |

### Touch

| Event | Response |
|-------|----------|
| touchstart | Enter Active state |
| touchend | Trigger action if touch ended within the button boundary |
| touchcancel | Return to Default state |

### Async behavior

When the button triggers an async operation (form submit, API call):
1. On trigger: enter Loading state immediately. `aria-busy="true"`. `pointer-events: none`.
2. On success: return to Default state. Update `aria-label` back to original. Trigger success feedback in context (toast, inline message — not the button itself).
3. On error: return to Default state (enabled). Error feedback is in context — button is available for retry.
4. On timeout (> 10s): return to Default state with error context. The button must not remain in Loading state indefinitely.

---

## 6. Do / Don't

| Do | Don't | Why |
|----|-------|-----|
| One Primary Button per visible surface | Two Primary Buttons side by side | Two primary buttons eliminate the visual hierarchy that guides users to the default path |
| Use Destructive + confirmation modal for irreversible actions | Use a plain Secondary button for destructive actions | The red Destructive variant signals danger; a grey button does not — users will click without understanding the consequence |
| Use Ghost for repetitive row-level actions in tables | Use Secondary or Primary for edit/view actions on every table row | Rows with Secondary/Primary buttons create an overwhelming sea of emphasis |
| Keep button labels to 1–3 words | Write full sentences as button labels | Long labels break button width uniformity and slow scanning |
| Use Loading state for all async triggers | Let a button appear clickable while its action is in-flight | Double-submitting forms or triggering actions twice is a common UX and data integrity problem |
| Pair Destructive buttons with a confirmation modal | Show Destructive action inline with no confirmation | Irreversible actions require a deliberate second confirmation — one accidental click should not cause data loss |

---

## 7. AI Generation Rules

### Generate

An AI agent operating on this spec may produce:
- All four variants (Primary, Secondary, Ghost, Destructive) in React TypeScript with CSS modules
- Both sizes (md, sm)
- Icon + label layout with Phosphor icon support (icon-left, icon-right positions)
- All interaction states implemented via CSS and React state
- Loading state with Phosphor `SpinnerGap` icon (animated via CSS `@keyframes spin`)
- Full ARIA markup: `aria-disabled`, `aria-busy`, `aria-label` for loading
- Storybook stories covering variant × state × size matrix
- Vitest unit tests for click, keyboard, disabled, and loading behavior

### Validate

Before approving any generated Button output, verify:
- [ ] All color values use `var(--color-*)` CSS custom properties — no hex or rgb literals
- [ ] All spacing values use `var(--spacing-*)` tokens — no raw px values
- [ ] Typography references `var(--typography-label-md)` — no raw font-size
- [ ] Hover state transitions use `var(--motion-duration-fast)` and `var(--motion-ease-standard)`
- [ ] Focus ring uses `var(--color-focus-ring)` + `var(--shadow-focus)` — visible in all variants
- [ ] Disabled state: `aria-disabled="true"` present, `pointer-events: none` applied, NOT using HTML `disabled` attribute alone
- [ ] Loading state: `aria-busy="true"`, `pointer-events: none`, spinner icon has `aria-hidden="true"`
- [ ] Touch target computed height ≥ 44px in md size, ≥ 36px is allowed in sm (but 44px preferred)
- [ ] Destructive variant uses `color-semantic-error` — not `color-action-primary` at red
- [ ] Each variant has a corresponding Storybook story

### Forbidden

An AI agent working on this spec must never:
- Generate a Button variant not in this spec (no "info", "warning", "success" button variants — use Toast and Alert components for those states)
- Use raw hex values anywhere in styles
- Apply `outline: none` or `outline: 0` without adding the replacement focus ring
- Generate `<a>` tags styled as Primary/Secondary buttons using this spec (links use `<a>` — this spec is `<button>` only)
- Use `opacity` as the mechanism for disabled state appearance
- Assume `<button type="submit">` — the type must be declared explicitly in the usage context, not hardcoded in the component
- Generate Loading state that disables all surrounding UI (loading is scoped to the button)

### Prompt Seed

```
Generate a Button component for Orbit (B2B analytics SaaS).

Reference: SDDn Behavior Spec ODS-BTN-L2-001 v2.0.0, inheriting from Foundation Spec ODS-L1-001 v1.0.0.

Framework: React TypeScript + CSS Modules
Icons: Phosphor React

Variants required: Primary, Secondary, Ghost, Destructive
Sizes: md (default), sm
Icon support: icon-left, icon-right optional slots
States per variant: default, hover, focus, active, disabled, loading

CSS custom property constraints (all values must use these):
- Primary background: var(--color-action-primary)
- Primary hover: var(--color-action-primary-dark)
- Secondary border: var(--color-border-default) → var(--color-border-strong) on hover
- Destructive: var(--color-semantic-error)
- Focus ring: var(--color-focus-ring) + var(--shadow-focus)
- All disabled text: var(--color-text-disabled)
- Padding (md): var(--spacing-2) var(--spacing-4)
- Radius: var(--radius-md)
- Font: var(--typography-label-md)
- Transition: var(--motion-duration-fast) var(--motion-ease-standard)

Loading: SpinnerGap from Phosphor, animated with CSS @keyframes spin, aria-hidden
Disabled: aria-disabled="true", pointer-events: none, NOT HTML disabled attribute

Do not generate: additional variants, raw hex values, <a>-as-button, opacity-only disabled.
```

---

## 8. Acceptance Criteria

- [ ] Primary variant renders with `var(--color-action-primary)` background in Default state
- [ ] Primary variant renders with `var(--color-action-primary-dark)` background in Hover state
- [ ] Secondary variant renders with `var(--color-border-default)` border in Default, `var(--color-border-strong)` in Hover
- [ ] Ghost variant background is transparent in Default, `var(--color-surface-base)` in Hover
- [ ] Destructive variant renders with `var(--color-semantic-error)` background in Default
- [ ] All variants: Focus state shows focus ring using `var(--color-focus-ring)` + `var(--shadow-focus)` tokens
- [ ] All variants: Disabled state — `aria-disabled="true"` present, click does not fire, pointer-events blocked
- [ ] All variants: Loading state — SpinnerGap icon renders, button non-interactive, `aria-busy="true"` present
- [ ] Keyboard: Tab reaches button, Enter activates it, Space activates it
- [ ] md size: computed height ≥ 44px
- [ ] Color contrast: Primary — white text on `color-action-primary` passes WCAG AA (4.5:1 minimum)
- [ ] Color contrast: Secondary — `color-text-primary` on `color-surface-raised` passes WCAG AA
- [ ] No raw hex values in generated styles
- [ ] Storybook: all variants × all states documented in stories

